// ============================================================
// Money (L6) — a Measure with convertible Units
// ============================================================
// A Measure declares a canonical unit (the starred one) and conversions to it. The lambda
// converts a value in that unit INTO the canonical, so `EUR: x -> $x * 1.09` reads as
// "one EUR is 1.09 USD".
//
// The important constraint, established from legend-engine rather than assumed: a
// unit-typed property CANNOT be mapped in a Relational mapping. No .pure file in
// legend-engine contains both `~mainTable` and `Measure`, and the relational compiler has
// no Unit handling. Units are mappable only through model-to-model (`Pure`) mappings,
// which is why this class hangs off the M2M layer and not off store::DB.
###Pure
Measure stress::Money
{
    *USD: x -> $x;
    EUR: x -> $x * 1.09;
    GBP: x -> $x * 1.27;
}

Class canonical::MonetaryTrade
{
    identifier: String[1];
    // A unit-typed property. It serialises as an OBJECT -- {"unit":[...],"value":n} --
    // never as a bare number, which is the whole point: the amount carries its unit.
    amount: stress::Money~USD[1];
}
